.TH STUDIO-1810C 1 "November 2026" "studio-1810c 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
studio-1810c \- mixer and routing control for the PreSonus / Fender Studio 1810c
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B studio-1810c
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a mixer window for the Studio 1810c audio interface. The window drives the
vendor USB protocol directly, so it can change the 18x10 routing matrix, the
output faders and the front-panel switches while the kernel driver keeps
streaming audio. Nothing needs to be unbound and playback keeps running.
.PP
The interface is opened through libusb. A udev rule installed with this package
grants members of the
.B plugdev
group and the logged-in desktop user access to it; if the rule is missing the
application offers to install it after an administrator prompt.
.PP
State is saved to
.I ~/.config/studio-1810c/state.json
and pushed to the device on demand. The matrix cannot be read back, so the
window marks a restored session as not pushed until you apply it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UC_APP_GEOM
Debugging aid: "X,Y,W,H" positions and pins the window so a screenshot can be
cropped deterministically. Not needed in normal use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/studio-1810c/
Application payload.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-presonus-1810c.rules
Device permission rule.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amixer (1),
.BR aplay (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Studio 1810c for Linux contributors.
